## PR Title
Configurable arbitrary integer clock divider

## PR Description
The existing `clk_div` clock divider module had critical limitations: it was not runtime-configurable and produced extremely unbalanced duty cycles. This PR introduces `clk_int_div`, a new module that guarantees 50% duty cycle output regardless of division factor (supporting both even and odd divisions). The design uses toggle flip-flops with 90 degree phase shift for odd divisions and features a valid-ready handshaked configuration interface that gates the clock during changes to prevent glitching. All sequential logic uses only the input clock, with output consisting exclusively of sequential elements and dedicated clock gating cells. The module includes a dedicated testbench and deprecates the legacy `clk_div` with optional warning messages during elaboration.

